program flow:

starts up through the command line from either the:
 - user
 - MCP server

program starts out with a given tablet size

if there are cells that are not selected yet, then we:
{
  user or program selects the next cell to work on
  
  displays the possible tiles to select from at that location
  
  user selects one of the tiles or randomely selects 1 of them
  
  updates the neighbors possible tiles
  
  visually displays the newly selected color
}

after the tablet is complete, have an option to export the image






-- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- 

command line arguments:
 - input image
 - tablet size
 - export & what filename to use


have a variable to store how many cell updates happen per frame displayed to screen
 - this will make the visual part of the application much more appealing


